{Suspect score - treat with caution...} 1. f4 e5 2. e4 exf4 3. Nf3 g5 4. h4 g4
5. Ne5 ({The bulletin printing a little unclear here - could be} 5. Ng5 Nf6 6.
Bc4 d5 7. exd5 Bg7 8. Nc3 Nh5 9. O-O {but} Be6 {still seems completely crazy})
5... Nf6 6. Bc4 d5 7. exd5 Bg7 8. Nc3 Nh5 9. d4 ({The bulletin gives} 9. O-O {
but this doesn't make any sense - it continues...} Be6 {This makes even less
sense...} 10. d4 Qxh4 11. Rxf4 Nxf4 12. Bxf4 g3 13. Qf3 Bxe5 14. Re1 {
Completely bonkers!} Bg4 15. Rxe5+ Kf8 16. Qxg3 Qxg3 17. Bh6+ {1-0. Instead I
have guessed at different moves 9 and 10, which make a bit more sense.}) 9...
Bf5 {This move a guess since ...Be6 makes no sense in any line.} 10. O-O Qxh4
11. Rxf4 Nxf4 12. Bxf4 g3 13. Qf3 Bxe5 ({The weak spot in my reconstruction is
that Black can probably play} 13... Qh2+ 14. Kf1 Qh1+ 15. Ke2 Qxa1 {- however,
it is the sort of line which a human might choose not to risk, given White's
powerful initiative for the rook.}) 14. Re1 Bg4 15. Rxe5+ Kf8 16. Qxg3 Qxg3 17.
Bh6+ 1-0

